From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Branson <andrew.branson@jolla.com>
Date: Thu, 21 May 2026 16:55:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Preload autoplay metadata before inaudible check

Blocked autoplay should still load enough metadata to determine whether the
media is audible.  On cellular, Sailfish uses a default preload action of
none, so an unmuted autoplay-only video can suspend before metadata is read.
If the file has no audio track, Gecko never learns that playback is actually
allowed and the element remains stuck on the poster/initial frame.

Use metadata preload for autoplay elements that are not yet allowed to play.
When metadata arrives, recompute the preload action so inaudible autoplay can
advance to normal playback.
---
 dom/html/HTMLMediaElement.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dom/html/HTMLMediaElement.cpp b/dom/html/HTMLMediaElement.cpp
index 399214d4c4f5..9830e61f676d 100644
--- a/dom/html/HTMLMediaElement.cpp
+++ b/dom/html/HTMLMediaElement.cpp
@@ -2949,6 +2949,8 @@ void HTMLMediaElement::UpdatePreloadAction() {
   // as we'll need it to play.
   if ((AllowedToPlay() && HasAttr(nsGkAtoms::autoplay)) || !mPaused) {
     nextAction = HTMLMediaElement::PRELOAD_ENOUGH;
+  } else if (HasAttr(kNameSpaceID_None, nsGkAtoms::autoplay)) {
+    nextAction = HTMLMediaElement::PRELOAD_METADATA;
   } else {
     // Find the appropriate preload action by looking at the attribute.
     const nsAttrValue* val =
@@ -5401,6 +5403,9 @@ void HTMLMediaElement::MetadataLoaded(const MediaInfo* aInfo,
   mTags = std::move(aTags);
   mLoadedDataFired = false;
   ChangeReadyState(HAVE_METADATA);
+  if (HasAttr(kNameSpaceID_None, nsGkAtoms::autoplay)) {
+    UpdatePreloadAction();
+  }
 
   // Add output tracks synchronously now to be sure they're available in
   // "loadedmetadata" event handlers.
